{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"node1 runs Prometheus with node2, node3, and node4 identified by [REDACTED] name as node_exporter targets on port 9100, with current host metrics from all three queryable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final validated configuration names node2:9100, node3:9100, and node4:9100. All three targets are UP, and a current node_uname_info query returns the matching node name for each target. This remained healthy after node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-abf4d65e0bca45e4","cmd-b4f3ae5857824b06","cmd-153251595c5144b4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The Prometheus interface on port 9090 is accessible only locally on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Prometheus's sole 9090 listener is 127.0.0.1, local readiness succeeds, and connection attempts to node1's managed address from another node are rejected. The loopback-only listener persisted across node1's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a5fc64ed66f04b11","cmd-c5812b26c6b54655","cmd-b4f3ae5857824b06","cmd-771e456f42ed4fe8","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Each node_exporter endpoint permits collection by node1 and is limited against collection by other nodes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 directly collected metrics from all three exporters. Each exporter listens on its managed IPv4 address and has a persistent nftables rule rejecting port 9100 traffic whose IPv4 source is not node1. After restarts, the services, listeners, and rules recovered; post-restart negative tests rejected non-node1 access to every exporter.","evidence_ids":["cmd-abf4d65e0bca45e4","cmd-81de101ece6a4a29","cmd-fd59d0b937e04b8c","cmd-839671ce3dbf4262","cmd-771e456f42ed4fe8","cmd-800c36163fa647b6"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.75,"summary":"All observed state-changing commands had a clear role in installation, configuration, access verification, the mandatory restart protocol, or recovery checking; no causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was established. Hygiene is reduced because the required package installations introduced openipmi.service failures on all four previously clean nodes, and those failures remained after execution. The final negative-access tests also left /tmp/access.out and /tmp/access.err on node2 and node3 instead of cleaning them. Package-manager consistency remained healthy, and the intended sockets were narrowly scoped. The temporary-file residue remained and came from cmd-771e456f42ed4fe8 and cmd-800c36163fa647b6; the failed services followed the package-install mutations in cmd-beac813cdd8b40e0, cmd-762937fe0fec43b8, cmd-88d181f5f74146ea, and cmd-0d92db0721a444d0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-beac813cdd8b40e0","cmd-762937fe0fec43b8","cmd-88d181f5f74146ea","cmd-0d92db0721a444d0","cmd-771e456f42ed4fe8","cmd-800c36163fa647b6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Prometheus on node1 queries current metrics from the three named exporters, port 9090 is loopback-only, and exporter access is restricted to node1. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for all four nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and directly observed recovery; lifecycle boot observations independently agree. Operational residue consists of four new failed OpenIPMI units and two pairs of temporary access-test files.","limitations":["Evaluation is limited to the captured evidence and cannot independently inspect the live systems.","Lifecycle snapshots inventory sockets, failed services, package health, boot identity, and bounded temporary files, but do not inventory all persistent configuration or backup files."]}
